# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
from fams import *
F = 'fbdis'
page('facebook-disabled-for-fake-name-appeal', F, 'Facebook Disabled for a Fake Name: How to Appeal',
 'Facebook disabled your account saying your name does not follow its rules? What the name policy asks for, which ID works and how to appeal.',
 'Facebook disabled your account over your name?', 'Disabled over name policy',
 'Facebook expects the name you use in daily life. Nicknames, stage names and business names are the usual triggers.',
 'Facebook disables profiles when the name looks fake or does not match how you are known. Appeal with an ID showing the name you use, or a document that shows the connection, such as a bank statement or utility bill, if the request lists them. Keep it short, and do not edit the name mid-process.',
 [('Use the daily name', 'The profile name should match what friends call you.'),
  ('Bring the proof the screen lists', 'ID first, other documents if offered.'),
  ('Do not edit mid-appeal', 'Changing the name while it is open can restart the review.')],
 [S('What triggers the name check', ul(['A nickname or an initial in place of a surname.', 'A business name used as a personal profile.', 'Symbols, titles or numbers in the name.', 'Reports from other users who think the name is fake.']),
    'Real people are flagged too, especially with names that are uncommon in the language of their country.'),
  S('How to appeal', ol(['Open the notice and choose the option to confirm your identity.', 'Upload the document the screen asks for, with the name matching your profile as closely as possible.', 'If the name differs, add a note on how the two connect.', 'Submit once, and keep a screenshot of the confirmation.']))],
 [('Can I use a nickname on Facebook?', 'You can add one as an additional name. The main name should be the one you use daily.'),
  ('What if my ID name is different?', 'Add a short explanation and, if offered, a second document that shows the name you use.'),
  ('Is a business better as a Page?', 'Yes. A business name belongs on a Page, not a personal profile.')],
 ['People with nicknames or stage names.', 'Owners using a business name on a profile.', 'People with uncommon names flagged by mistake.'])

page('facebook-disabled-after-posting-in-groups', F, 'Facebook Disabled After Posting in Groups',
 'Facebook disabled your profile after you posted the same message in many groups? Why group posting looks like spam and how to appeal.',
 'Facebook disabled after posting in groups?', 'Disabled after group posting',
 'Posting the same thing across many groups is a common cause of a sudden disabling. Here is what to do.',
 'Facebook treats the same post sent to many groups in a short time as spam, even when each group allows it. The profile can be disabled, especially if group admins also reported it. Stop the posting, appeal by confirming your identity, and describe plainly that you were sharing your own content or business, not running automation.',
 [('Stop the cross-posting', 'Pause group posting while the appeal is open.'),
  ('Say what you posted', 'Honest detail on the content helps.'),
  ('Check group rules', 'Some groups ban promotions, and admins can report.')],
 [S('What the pattern looks like', ul(['The same text and link posted into many groups in a short stretch.', 'Repeated joining of new groups.', 'Reports from admins or members for self-promotion.', 'Automated posting tools.']),
    'Sellers and event promoters are most affected.'),
  S('Appeal steps', ol(['Open the notice and verify your identity as asked.', 'Explain what you were posting and where, in a few sentences.', 'Remove duplicate posts that remain.', 'Keep group posting slow and varied after access returns.']))],
 [('Will the groups lose me?', 'Group memberships can return with the account. It depends on the outcome.'),
  ('Is a scheduler tool allowed?', 'Official tools are one thing. Anything that logs in for you or posts in bulk can cause flags.'),
  ('Should I tell the group admins?', 'No. Wait for the result and focus on the appeal.')],
 ['Sellers and promoters.', 'Community managers.', 'People who joined and posted in many groups.'])

page('facebook-disabled-suspicious-activity-appeal', F, 'Facebook Disabled for Suspicious Activity: What Now',
 'Facebook says your account was disabled for suspicious activity? What triggers this notice and what you can send to confirm it is really you.',
 'Facebook disabled for suspicious activity?', 'Disabled for suspicious activity',
 'This notice is generic. It fits a login from a new place, a bulk action or a hack. Work out which.',
 'Suspicious activity covers many things, from a login in a new country to many actions in a short time. First decide which fits: a hack, a tool or a new device. Then confirm your identity through the notice, state what you think triggered it, and keep activity calm after access returns.',
 [('Find the cause', 'Think about what you did differently before it started.'),
  ('Confirm your identity', 'Follow the steps on the notice with a clear ID.'),
  ('Keep it calm after', 'Avoid bursts of actions once it is back.')],
 [S('Typical triggers', ul(['A login from a new country, device or VPN.', 'Bursts of friend requests, messages or posts.', 'A hacker using the account.', 'A tool or extension acting on the profile.'])),
  S('What to do', ol(['Open the notice and complete the identity steps.', 'Write a short explanation of what you were doing, based on your own recall.', 'Remove tools and log out of unknown sessions if you can reach them.', 'If the account was hacked, say so clearly.']))],
 [('Is this the same as being banned?', 'Not necessarily. Many of these are security locks that clear after verification.'),
  ('Do I need to send ID?', 'Only if the notice asks. Use the official screen.'),
  ('What if there is no appeal button?', 'Check the email on the account and use the help flow for a disabled account.')],
 ['People who got a generic notice.', 'Travellers and VPN users.', 'Accounts that may have been hacked.'])

page('facebook-disabled-marketplace-scam-flag', F, 'Facebook Disabled After a Marketplace Scam Report',
 'Facebook disabled your account after a buyer reported your Marketplace listing? How reports lead to disabling and how to appeal as a genuine seller.',
 'Facebook disabled after Marketplace reports?', 'Disabled after Marketplace reports',
 'Selling on Marketplace attracts reports, some genuine and some not. Here is how to respond.',
 'A buyer’s scam report, a listing flagged as prohibited, or many listings at once can lead Facebook to disable a seller’s account. Appeal by confirming your identity, and describe what you sell, with any receipts, delivery records or chat history that show real orders. Do not create a second account to continue selling.',
 [('Show real sales', 'Receipts and delivery proof support the appeal.'),
  ('Check your listings', 'Remove anything that could be read as prohibited.'),
  ('Do not open a second account', 'It can lead to further bans.')],
 [S('Why sellers get flagged', ul(['A buyer reports non-delivery or a fake item.', 'Listings in restricted categories.', 'Many listings posted at once.', 'Offers that look too good to be true, or copied photos.']),
    'Genuine sellers are caught too, particularly with high-volume listings.'),
  S('What to prepare', ol(['Gather proof of orders, such as chats, payment confirmations and tracking numbers.', 'Review your listings for categories that are not allowed.', 'Open the notice and verify your identity.', 'Explain in a few lines what you sell and how orders are fulfilled.']))],
 [('Will paying the buyer back help?', 'It can show good faith, but it is up to the review.'),
  ('Can I list again after it returns?', 'Yes, but slowly. Avoid posting many listings at once.'),
  ('What about the buyer who reported me?', 'Do not contact them again. Let the appeal run.')],
 ['Marketplace sellers.', 'Small shops that use Marketplace for sales.', 'Resellers with many listings.'])

page('facebook-disabled-id-upload-rejected-again', F, 'Facebook ID Upload Rejected Again After a Disable',
 'Facebook keeps rejecting the ID you upload to confirm your identity? Frequent reasons, such as glare, cropping or the wrong document, and how to retry.',
 'Facebook keeps rejecting your ID upload?', 'ID upload rejected again',
 'A rejected upload does not close the matter; it just asks for a better one. Fix the cause before sending it again.',
 'Facebook rejects ID uploads that are blurry, cropped, expired or show a different name from the profile. Photograph the original document on a plain surface in good light, with all corners visible and no glare. If the rejection repeats, check the name and the document type against the list on the request screen before trying again.',
 [('Plain surface and good light', 'No glare, no shadows across the text.'),
  ('All corners visible', 'Do not crop the edges.'),
  ('Check the list', 'The request screen names the documents it accepts.')],
 [S('What leads to a rejection', ul(['Glare on the plastic or lamination.', 'A photo of a screen or a photocopy.', 'A different name from the profile name, with no explanation.', 'An expired or unsupported document type.']),
    'Each rejection should show a reason. Read it and fix that one thing.'),
  S('How to retry', ol(['Place the document on a dark, plain surface and use daylight.', 'Take a straight-on photo, without flash.', 'Check that the name and date of birth are readable.', 'Upload once and wait for the answer.']))],
 [('How many times can I upload?', 'There may be a limit. Make each try a careful one.'),
  ('What if my name differs from the profile?', 'Explain the link in the note, and use a second document if the screen offers one.'),
  ('Can I send the ID to Unbanz?', 'No. Upload it only on the official screen.')],
 ['People who got a rejection message.', 'Owners with a laminated ID.', 'Anyone whose name differs from the ID.'])

page('facebook-disabled-under-age-flag', F, 'Facebook Disabled Because It Thinks You Are Under 13',
 'Facebook disabled your account over your age, even though you are an adult? How the age check works, what to send and what cannot be fixed.',
 'Facebook disabled your account over your age?', 'Disabled over an age flag',
 'Age flags come from a birthday entered long ago, a mistake, or a joke date. Adults can fix this with proof.',
 'Facebook disables accounts it believes belong to someone under the minimum age, often because of a wrong birth year entered at sign-up. If you are an adult, the appeal asks for ID showing your real date of birth. If you really are under the age, the rule applies and an appeal cannot change that.',
 [('Check the date of birth', 'A typo years ago is the usual cause.'),
  ('Send proof of age', 'An accepted ID that shows the date of birth.'),
  ('Rules apply to everyone', 'Under the minimum age, an appeal will not work.')],
 [S('How it happens', ul(['A birth year entered wrongly at sign-up.', 'A joke or placeholder date.', 'Reports from other users about age.', 'Content in the profile that suggests a young user.'])),
  S('How to appeal', ol(['Open the notice and select the option to confirm your age.', 'Upload an ID that shows your date of birth, as the screen asks.', 'If the date on file is wrong, say so in a line.', 'Submit once and wait.']),
    'We cannot help with accounts that belong to someone under the minimum age.')],
 [('Can the date of birth be changed after?', 'If the account is restored, you may be able to correct it. Rules limit how often it can be changed.'),
  ('Does a parent need to send ID?', 'The account holder’s own ID is what counts, and the age rule applies.'),
  ('Does the account come back?', 'That is Facebook’s decision.')],
 ['Adults with a wrong birth year on file.', 'People whose accounts are very old.', 'Owners who entered a placeholder date.'])

page('facebook-disabled-after-hack-used-for-spam', F, 'Facebook Disabled After a Hacker Used It for Spam',
 'Your Facebook was hacked, spam went out, and now the account is disabled? How to sort out the order of recovery and appeal.',
 'Facebook hacked then disabled for spam?', 'Hacked then disabled',
 'A hacker’s activity can get your profile disabled, which makes a hack look like a violation. You can separate them.',
 'When a hacker posts spam from your profile, Facebook can disable it for the activity. Treat it as a hack first: secure your email, change passwords, and use the hacked-account route. Then appeal the disabling and say clearly that you did not send the spam, with dates of when you lost control.',
 [('Secure the email first', 'Your email is the key to the account.'),
  ('Say it was a hack', 'In both the recovery and the appeal.'),
  ('Give dates', 'When you last used it and when you noticed.')],
 [S('Why the two overlap', ul(['The hacker posts links or messages to many people.', 'Reports arrive from the people who received them.', 'The system flags the account for the behavior.', 'The email or phone may be changed, so notices do not reach you.'])),
  S('What to do', ol(['Change the email password and enable two-factor on it.', 'Use the hacked-account flow for Facebook.', 'Appeal the disabling, with dates and a short account of what you saw.', 'Warn friends by another channel not to click anything.']))],
 [('Can the spam posts be removed?', 'After recovery you can delete them. The appeal itself does not need that.'),
  ('Will friends be blocked from me?', 'Not by Facebook. They may unfriend you after seeing spam.'),
  ('Does Unbanz log in to clean it up?', 'No. We never log in. You do that after access returns.')],
 ['People whose friends got spam from them.', 'Owners with a changed email.', 'Accounts that went from hacked to disabled.'])

page('facebook-disabled-while-travelling', F, 'Facebook Disabled While You Were Travelling',
 'Facebook disabled or locked your account after you logged in abroad or on a new network? Why travel triggers it and how to confirm it is you.',
 'Facebook disabled while travelling?', 'Disabled while travelling',
 'A login from another country looks like a takeover until you confirm it. Here is how to do that.',
 'A login from a new country, a hotel network or a VPN can lock or disable a Facebook account until you confirm it is you. Use your own phone if you can, complete the identity steps in order, and explain in the notes that you were travelling. Avoid several tries from different networks at once.',
 [('Use your own phone', 'A known device passes more easily.'),
  ('One network, one try', 'Do not jump between networks.'),
  ('Say you were travelling', 'A short line in the note helps.')],
 [S('What triggers it', ul(['Roaming or a new local SIM.', 'Hotel or airport networks that many people share.', 'A VPN switched on while abroad.', 'Logging in from a laptop you have not used before.'])),
  S('What to try', ol(['Go back to your usual phone and a stable connection.', 'Open the notice and finish each step, including any code or ID request.', 'Add a note saying you were travelling and where.', 'If you are locked out entirely, contact us with the screenshots.']))],
 [('Will it happen again?', 'It can. Turn on two-factor and add a trusted device before you travel.'),
  ('What if the code goes to my home number?', 'Roaming may block it. Use an email option, or an authenticator app, if it is set up.'),
  ('Can I appeal remotely?', 'Yes. The appeal does not depend on where you are.')],
 ['Travellers and expats.', 'People using hotel Wi-Fi.', 'Anyone who used a VPN abroad.'])

page('facebook-disabled-page-admin-lost-pages', F, 'Facebook Profile Disabled and You Lost Access to Your Pages',
 'Your personal Facebook profile was disabled and your Pages and ad accounts went with it? How admin roles work and what to do to regain control.',
 'Facebook profile disabled and Pages lost?', 'Profile disabled, Pages lost',
 'Pages are managed through a personal profile or a business portfolio. If the profile goes, access can too.',
 'If your profile is disabled and you were the only admin of a Page, you can lose access to the Page and its ad account. Check whether other admins exist, whether the Page sits in a business portfolio, and whether a second person can add you as admin. Appeal the profile at the same time.',
 [('Ask other admins', 'Anyone with full control can add you back.'),
  ('Check the portfolio', 'Pages inside a portfolio can have a second login route.'),
  ('Appeal the profile', 'Restoring it brings back its Page roles.')],
 [S('How roles are tied', ul(['A Page admin role belongs to a profile.', 'A business portfolio can hold Pages and ad accounts with other admins.', 'If you were the only admin, there may be no one to restore access.', 'Ad accounts follow the same pattern.']),
    'This is the reason to set up a second admin before anything goes wrong.'),
  S('What to do', ol(['Check whether any other person is admin of the Page, and ask them to add you or your new profile.', 'Look for the business portfolio and who else is in it.', 'Appeal the disabled profile with an identity check.', 'Send us the Page link and the situation, and we will look at what fits.']))],
 [('Can I make a new profile and become admin again?', 'Only if an existing admin adds you. Without one, the route is harder.'),
  ('Should I worry about the ad account?', 'If ads were running, the payment method still bills. Check the billing information.'),
  ('Does Unbanz work on Pages?', 'We help with the access request. The decision belongs to Facebook.')],
 ['Business owners who used a personal profile as admin.', 'Agencies that lost a client Page.', 'Anyone with a Page that has one admin.'])

page('facebook-disabled-after-friend-request-spam', F, 'Facebook Disabled After Sending Many Friend Requests',
 'Facebook disabled your account after you sent lots of friend requests or messages? How the limits work and how to appeal with an honest explanation.',
 'Facebook disabled after many friend requests?', 'Disabled after friend requests',
 'Sending requests to strangers in bulk is read as spam. A normal user does not do that.',
 'Facebook disables accounts that send many friend requests to people they do not know, especially when several are ignored or reported. Stop the requests, appeal by confirming your identity, and explain why you were reaching out, for example to grow a local business or find old classmates. Avoid sending more once it returns.',
 [('Stop the outreach', 'Do not send more requests while it is open.'),
  ('Explain the purpose', 'A reason such as local business helps.'),
  ('Return slowly', 'Keep requests to people you know afterwards.')],
 [S('How it is judged', ul(['Many requests to strangers in a short stretch.', 'Many ignored or reported requests.', 'Identical messages to new contacts.', 'A new account sending requests right away.']),
    'Facebook does not publish exact limits.'),
  S('Appeal steps', ol(['Open the notice and confirm your identity.', 'Write what the requests were for in two lines.', 'Remove tools that send requests automatically.', 'Keep a calm routine after it returns.']))],
 [('Can I add people through groups instead?', 'Joining and taking part in groups is allowed. Do not copy-paste the same message to everyone.'),
  ('Will old friends remain?', 'They come back if the account is restored.'),
  ('What about a business Page?', 'A Page is better for reaching strangers than a personal profile.')],
 ['Small business owners growing a network.', 'Community admins.', 'People who tried to reconnect with many contacts.'])
